### MG Lab #5 — least-privilege Graph access for the managed identity (run in Graph Explorer as an admin)
### Use the USER-ASSIGNED identity (graphIdentityPrincipalId / graphIdentityClientId outputs of main.bicep).
### Grant BEFORE the function first calls Graph: managed identity tokens are cached for up to 24 hours.
### 1. Find the identity's service principal
GET https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{principalId}?$select=id,appId,displayName

### 2. Find Microsoft Graph's service principal and the Sites.Selected app role id
GET https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/servicePrincipals(appId='00000003-0000-0000-c000-000000000000')?$select=id,appRoles

### 3. Give the identity the Sites.Selected application permission (appRoleId 883ea226-0bf2-4a8f-9f9d-92c9162a727d)
POST https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{principalId}/appRoleAssignments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "principalId": "{principalId}", "resourceId": "{graphServicePrincipalId}", "appRoleId": "883ea226-0bf2-4a8f-9f9d-92c9162a727d" }

### 4. Grant READ on ONE site only (Sites.Selected = no access until a site grants it)
POST https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/sites/{siteId}/permissions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roles": ["read"], "grantedToIdentities": [ { "application": { "id": "{graphIdentityClientId}", "displayName": "func-mglab-graph" } } ] }

### 5. Check
GET https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/sites/{siteId}/permissions
